  "steps": [
    "Vinaigrette: blend the harissa, vinegar, olive oil, water, garlic, honey, and salt until smooth. Add more water a tablespoon at a time if it is too thick. Set aside.",
    "Pat the chicken dry and season both sides with the Meat & Potatoes seasoning.",
    "Heat a grill pan or skillet over medium-high heat and brush with the vegetable oil. Cook the chicken until browned and 165°F in the thickest part, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Rest 5 minutes, then slice.",
    "Toss the cucumber and tomatoes with the olive oil and sea salt.",
    "Divide the lettuce and rice among 4 bowls. Add the cucumber-tomato mix, pickled onions, feta, and chicken, then a scoop each of hummus and tzatziki.",
    "Top with cilantro and red pepper flakes, drizzle with the vinaigrette, and serve with pita on the side."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "The original lists the bowl toppings for a single bowl alongside 1 lb of chicken; the bowl amounts here are multiplied by four so all the chicken gets used.",
    "Brown rice takes 30 minutes or more to cook, so make it ahead; the 40 minute total assumes it is ready."
  ],
